# How linux/ borneo/dev splits into upstream series, read by tools/mkseries.
#
#   series NAME          starts a series
#   hold REASON          mkseries reports it as not ready to send, and says why
#   needs NAME           apply that series first, without emitting its patches
#   SUBJECT              a commit on borneo/dev, by subject, in applying order
#
# Every commit on the branch has to appear here exactly once, so nothing gets forgotten.

# Fixes that stand alone, each to its own maintainers.

series asoc-q6-fixes
ASoC: qcom: q6asm-dai: Report 24-bit PCM as S32_LE
ASoC: qcom: q6dsp-lpass-clocks: Set drvdata before registering clocks

series bt-hci-qca-retry
Bluetooth: hci_qca: Leave the chip off for a while before retrying

series ath10k-assoc-bw
wifi: ath10k: Handle a channel change before the vdev is up

series ath10k-pipe-leak
wifi: ath10k: snoc: Free the pipes when allocating them fails
wifi: ath10k: pci: Free the pipes when allocating them fails

series ath10k-thermal-unregister
wifi: ath10k: Unregister the cooling device during a firmware start

series qmi-txn-lifetime
soc: qcom: qmi: Don't use a transaction after its waiter has returned

series serdev-tty-mutex
serdev: ttyport: Hold tty_mutex while setting up the tty

series fastrpc-remove-lock
misc: fastrpc: Don't take a user's lock under the channel's

series fastrpc-interrupted
needs fastrpc-remove-lock
hold Anandu Krishnan E's patch: v2 was asked to rebase and they promised a new version. Report the crash, v2's dropped reference and this version to them first, rather than racing them
misc: fastrpc: Don't send an interrupted call to the DSP again

series sm6115-adsp-lpi-votes
remoteproc: qcom_q6v5_pas: Hold the LPI domains while the SM6115 ADSP boots
arm64: dts: qcom: sm6115: Name the ADSP's power domains
arm64: dts: qcom: agatti: Name the ADSP's power domains

series lpass-dsp-restart
needs asoc-q6-fixes
needs sm6115-adsp-lpi-votes
hold RFC first: crosses PM, SoundWire, ASoC and pinctrl, so the design needs the maintainers' view, and a debugfs crash during a stream still resets the phone
PM: clk: Report a clock that fails to enable
soundwire: qcom: Don't touch the controller without its clock
ASoC: qcom: qdsp6: Keep the audio clocks across a DSP restart
pinctrl: qcom: lpass-lpi: Restore the pins after a DSP restart
soundwire: qcom: Set the controller up again after a DSP restart

series input-pm8xxx-vib
Input: pm8xxx-vibrator - Write the voltage's high bits

series msm-dsi-phy-sleep
drm/msm/dsi: Suspend the PHY during system sleep

series watchdog-qcom-sleep
watchdog: qcom: Stop during system sleep if running but not opened

series glink-smem-wake
rpmsg: glink: smem: Allow messages to wake the system

series gcc-sm6115-usb
clk: qcom: gcc-sm6115: Use retention for USB power domain

series pmdomain-fixes
pmdomain: core: Free subdomain links outside the genpd locks
pmdomain: core: Wait for a genpd's device links before it can be freed

series cpuidle-name-leak
cpuidle: psci: Free the name of a PM domain when removing it
cpuidle: riscv-sbi: Free the name of a PM domain when removing it

series leds-qcom-flash-fixes
leds: flash: leds-qcom-flash: Keep the mutex until the LEDs are gone
leds: flash: leds-qcom-flash: Release the V4L2 flash devices properly

series smbx-epc-sem
power: supply: qcom_smbx: Don't go through the core to read the status

series pinconf-generic-alloc
pinctrl: pinconf-generic: Check the bitmap allocation in parse_fw_cfg()

series udmabuf-seg-size
dma-buf/udmabuf: Don't limit the misc device to 64K DMA segments

series camss-fixes
media: qcom: camss: Don't limit buffers to 64K DMA segments
media: qcom: camss: Don't create sensor links again on a rebind
media: qcom: camss: Don't offer to unbind through sysfs
media: qcom: camss: Prepare the shared clocks only while in use

series dw9719-fixes
media: i2c: dw9719: Go all the way back to the position on resume
media: i2c: dw9719: Turn the supply off when detection fails

series v4l2-register-media
media: v4l2-core: Fail to register a video device without its media parts

series v4l2-subdev-unregister
media: v4l2-subdev: Don't use what unregistering clears

series s5k-selection-height
media: i2c: s5k3m5: Report the crop height, not the width, as the height
media: i2c: s5kjn1: Report the crop height, not the width, as the height

series ipa-modem-boot-power
net: ipa: Keep the IPA powered while the modem boots, every time

# SM6115, each independent of the board.

series sm6115-dispcc-ao
dt-bindings: clock: qcom,sm6115-dispcc: Add the active-only XO
clk: qcom: dispcc-sm6115: Run the AHB clock from the active-only XO
arm64: dts: qcom: sm6115: Give dispcc the active-only XO

series sm6115-mdss-ahb
dt-bindings: display: msm: qcom,sm6115-mdss: Add the dispcc AHB clock
arm64: dts: qcom: sm6115: Give MDSS the display AHB clock

series sm6115-power
arm64: dts: qcom: sm6115: Fix CPU cluster idle state parameters
arm64: dts: qcom: sm6115: Hook up MPM
arm64: dts: qcom: sm6115: Add a system power domain
arm64: dts: qcom: sm6115: Add RPM master stats

series sm6115-ipa
dt-bindings: net: qcom,ipa: Add SM6115
arm64: dts: qcom: sm6115: Add IPA

series sm6115-audio
hold Klimov's and Dybcio's patches are theirs: check whether they are still working on them
arm64: dts: qcom: sm6115: Set up CPU cooling maps
arm64: dts: qcom: sm6115: add LPASS devices
arm64: dts: qcom: sm4250: add description of soundwire and dmic pins
arm64: dts: qcom: sm6115: Use the VA macro's own compatible

# Drivers.

series panel-ft8009
dt-bindings: display: panel: Add DJN FT8009
drm/panel: Add DJN FT8009 panel driver

series moto-smem-board
